INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (460009382102015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”, how should Filtration theory be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”, how should Rotary drum filter etc. Batch sedimentation test be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”, how should Theory of centrifugal separation be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] In a practical situation within “Size Reduction and Screening”, how should Classification of size reduction equipments be applied? Explain the method, identify the governing conditions and justify the expected result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Filtration retains particles on or in a porous medium while fluid passes through; pressure drop and cake resistance affect rate.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence, including the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or formulas from “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”. Relate it to Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation; Definition and Mechanisms of filtration; Filter media and filter aids; Classification & Selection of filtration equipments. Where a numerical relationship is required, define the quantities, use consistent units and state the operating assumptions.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a chemical-engineering process, laboratory task or equipment-selection problem within “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”. State the expected outcome and why the chosen approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the required process condition or design objective and mention a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Sedimentation separates suspended particles by gravitational settling, with performance affected by particle size, density difference and fluid properties.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence, including the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or formulas from “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”. Relate it to Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation; Definition and Mechanisms of filtration; Filtration theory; Filter media and filter aids. Where a numerical relationship is required, define the quantities, use consistent units and state the operating assumptions.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a chemical-engineering process, laboratory task or equipment-selection problem within “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”. State the expected outcome and why the chosen approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the required process condition or design objective and mention a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Filtration retains particles on or in a porous medium while fluid passes through; pressure drop and cake resistance affect rate.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence, including the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or formulas from “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”. Relate it to Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation; Definition and Mechanisms of filtration; Filtration theory; Filter media and filter aids. Where a numerical relationship is required, define the quantities, use consistent units and state the operating assumptions.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a chemical-engineering process, laboratory task or equipment-selection problem within “Filtration, Sedimentation and Centrifugal Separation”. State the expected outcome and why the chosen approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the required process condition or design objective and mention a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Size reduction reduces particles using mechanical forces; the required size, energy use and material properties determine equipment selection.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence, including the relevant process steps, variables, equipment or formulas from “Size Reduction and Screening”. Relate it to Size Reduction and Screening; Crushing Law; Crushers; Grinders. Where a numerical relationship is required, define the quantities, use consistent units and state the operating assumptions.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply the concept to a chemical-engineering process, laboratory task or equipment-selection problem within “Size Reduction and Screening”. State the expected outcome and why the chosen approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the required process condition or design objective and mention a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

